---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Rindow">
  <section class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">PHP libraries for practical computing</p><h1>Build more with Rindow</h1><p>Machine learning, mathematics, and application frameworks designed to work together.</p><div><a class="button" href="/neuralnetworks/index.html">Explore Neural Networks</a><a class="button secondary" href="/mathematics/index.html">Browse Mathematics</a></div></section>
  <section class="cards">
    <article><img src="/assets/themes/rindow/img/brain.svg" alt="" /><h2>Neural Networks</h2><p>Deep learning tools for PHP, from familiar layers to high-performance computing.</p><a href="/neuralnetworks/index.html">View documentation →</a></article>
    <article><img src="/assets/themes/rindow/img/graph.svg" alt="" /><h2>Mathematics</h2><p>Matrix operations, numerical libraries, plotting, and acceleration options.</p><a href="/mathematics/index.html">View documentation →</a></article>
    <article><img src="/assets/themes/rindow/img/gears.svg" alt="" /><h2>Framework</h2><p>Modular PHP application architecture with IoC, DI, and AOP support.</p><a href="/framework/index.html">View documentation →</a></article>
  </section>
  <section class="principles" aria-label="What Rindow stands for">
    <article class="principle">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Practical freedom</p><h2>Off the chain</h2><p>Everyone will tell us, “Do you have to use PHP for machine learning?” Experience the processing speed and portability of Rindow. Here is the answer: leave common sense behind and step into a new world.</p></div>
      <img src="/assets/themes/rindow/img/mnist.png" alt="Off the chain" />
    </article>
    <article class="principle reverse">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Healthy systems</p><h2>Decluttering</h2><p>Are those who ridicule monoliths free from the spell of modules? The essence of modularization is neither reuse nor distributed development. Separating and discarding parts keeps the whole system healthy.</p></div>
      <img src="/assets/themes/rindow/img/gears.svg" alt="Decluttering" />
    </article>
    <article class="principle">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Open by design</p><h2>Interoperability</h2><p>Rindow aims to replace itself with others. What remains when it is gone is the definition of the interface. We build toward interfaces that are independent of Rindow—and a new standard anyone can join.</p></div>
      <img src="/assets/themes/rindow/img/microservices.svg" alt="Interoperability" />
    </article>
  </section>
</Base>
